{"matches":[{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-q7v9-x93c-xqv3","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-q7v9-x93c-xqv3","namespace":"github:language:rust","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-q7v9-x93c-xqv3","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115909","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/pull/984","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/a543a1fc8f3f3eef36f27bb137230295284cdb98","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.0"],"description":"zip: Unbounded Symlink-Target Handling Can Abort Or Exhaust Memory During Extraction","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115909","epss":0.00461,"percentile":0.39973,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115909","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115909","cwe":"CWE-789","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["9.0.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"9.0.0","date":"2026-10-30","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.34575000000000006},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-115909","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115909","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/a543a1fc8f3f3eef36f27bb137230295284cdb98","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/pull/984","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.0","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-q7v9-x93c-xqv3"],"description":"zip is a zip library for Rust that supports reading and writing simple ZIP files. From 1.3.0 until 9.0.0, ZipArchive::extract in src/read/mod.rs calls Vec::with_capacity for a symbolic link target using the attacker-controlled ZIP64 uncompressed_size before reading entry data. A small archive can request an impossible capacity, causing the infallible allocation path to abort the process before the entry is validated. The failure cannot be contained with catch_unwind or a worker thread, allowing repeated denial of service in archive-processing applications. This issue is fixed in version 9.0.0.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115909","epss":0.00461,"percentile":0.39973,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115909","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115909","cwe":"CWE-789","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"rust-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"rust","namespace":"github:language:rust","package":{"name":"zip","version":"8.6.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-q7v9-x93c-xqv3","versionConstraint":">=1.3.0,<9.0.0 (unknown)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"9.0.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index#zip@8.6.0","name":"zip","version":"8.6.0","type":"rust-crate","locations":null,"language":"rust","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:cargo/zip@8.6.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-hjqx-j4rw-g7xv","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hjqx-j4rw-g7xv","namespace":"github:language:rust","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-hjqx-j4rw-g7xv","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115908","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/09c030eab56e8db8fb3c1c33f554407b30bad8fa","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.0"],"description":"zip: Arbitrary file write outside the extraction directory, because ZipArchive::extract validates symlink targets lexically.","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.4,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":5.2},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115908","epss":0.00432,"percentile":0.37566,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115908","cwe":"CWE-22","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115908","cwe":"CWE-59","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115908","cwe":"CWE-61","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["9.0.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"9.0.0","date":"2026-10-30","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.32184},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-115908","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115908","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/09c030eab56e8db8fb3c1c33f554407b30bad8fa","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.0","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-hjqx-j4rw-g7xv"],"description":"zip is a zip library for Rust that supports reading and writing simple ZIP files. From 7.2.0 until 9.0.0, ZipArchive::extract and ZipArchive::extract_unwrapped_root_dir use safe_prepare_path in src/read/zipfile.rs and simplified_components in src/path.rs to validate symbolic link targets with a lexical prefix comparison rather than resolving each intermediate link. An attacker who knows or can guess the absolute extraction destination can create a chain whose apparent target remains under the destination while an intermediate symlink resolves outside it, allowing attacker-controlled files to be created or overwritten with the extracting process's privileges. On Windows, discarded drive and UNC prefixes can permit a single-link escape when the process has SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege, such as through administrator rights or Developer Mode. This regression is distinct from CVE-2025-29787. This issue is fixed in version 9.0.0.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.4,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":5.2},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115908","epss":0.00432,"percentile":0.37566,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115908","cwe":"CWE-22","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115908","cwe":"CWE-59","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115908","cwe":"CWE-61","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"rust-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"rust","namespace":"github:language:rust","package":{"name":"zip","version":"8.6.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-hjqx-j4rw-g7xv","versionConstraint":">=7.2.0,<9.0.0 (unknown)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"9.0.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index#zip@8.6.0","name":"zip","version":"8.6.0","type":"rust-crate","locations":null,"language":"rust","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:cargo/zip@8.6.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-m665-v7pm-7grj","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-m665-v7pm-7grj","namespace":"github:language:rust","severity":"Critical","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-m665-v7pm-7grj","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115905","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/8068ab480ccf8daa7411424e365fcdbe6d09443e","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.5"],"description":"zip: Critical Parser Differential & Security Control Bypass via Dual-Header Inconsistencies (Zip Cloaking) Leading to Arbitrary File Overwrite & RCE","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:L","metrics":{"baseScore":10},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115905","epss":0.0032,"percentile":0.25012,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115905","cwe":"CWE-20","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115905","cwe":"CWE-436","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"}],"fix":{"versions":["9.0.5"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"9.0.5","date":"2026-10-29","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.304},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-115905","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115905","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Critical","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/8068ab480ccf8daa7411424e365fcdbe6d09443e","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.5","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-m665-v7pm-7grj"],"description":"zip is a zip library for Rust that supports reading and writing simple ZIP files. Through 9.0.4, ZipArchive treats Central Directory File Header filenames as authoritative while ZipStreamReader extracts using Local File Header filenames without reconciling the duplicate metadata in src/read/stream.rs. A crafted archive can therefore appear benign to a component that inspects the central directory but cause a streaming extractor to write a different attacker-selected path and content, potentially overwriting files used by a downstream service. This issue is fixed in version 9.0.5.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:L/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","metrics":{"baseScore":10},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115905","epss":0.0032,"percentile":0.25012,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115905","cwe":"CWE-20","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115905","cwe":"CWE-436","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"rust-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"rust","namespace":"github:language:rust","package":{"name":"zip","version":"8.6.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-m665-v7pm-7grj","versionConstraint":"<=9.0.4 (unknown)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"9.0.5"}}],"artifact":{"id":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index#zip@8.6.0","name":"zip","version":"8.6.0","type":"rust-crate","locations":null,"language":"rust","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:cargo/zip@8.6.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-9hj8-73fh-9963","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9hj8-73fh-9963","namespace":"github:language:rust","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-9hj8-73fh-9963","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115907","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/pull/991","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/8b4991288b79ad11cce201c2d785d5baa795bd3e","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.0"],"description":"zip: legacy Shrink/Reduce/Implode decoder: denial of service from attacker-controlled ZIP64 uncompressed size","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115907","epss":0.0035,"percentile":0.28675,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115907","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115907","cwe":"CWE-789","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["9.0.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"9.0.0","date":"2026-10-30","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.2625},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-115907","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115907","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/8b4991288b79ad11cce201c2d785d5baa795bd3e","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/pull/991","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.0","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-9hj8-73fh-9963"],"description":"zip is a zip library for Rust that supports reading and writing simple ZIP files. From 5.1.0 until 9.0.0, applications built with the legacy-zip feature can reserve output capacity from an attacker-controlled ZIP64 uncompressed size before validating the compressed stream. The ShrinkDecoder path in src/legacy/shrink.rs can panic with a capacity overflow during ZipArchive::extract, and the Reduce and Implode decoders contain the same unbounded preallocation pattern. An unhandled panic can terminate an archive-processing service. This issue is fixed in version 9.0.0.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115907","epss":0.0035,"percentile":0.28675,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115907","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115907","cwe":"CWE-789","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"rust-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"rust","namespace":"github:language:rust","package":{"name":"zip","version":"8.6.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-9hj8-73fh-9963","versionConstraint":">=5.1.0,<9.0.0 (unknown)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"9.0.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index#zip@8.6.0","name":"zip","version":"8.6.0","type":"rust-crate","locations":null,"language":"rust","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:cargo/zip@8.6.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-8hxf-qr8p-62x4","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8hxf-qr8p-62x4","namespace":"github:language:rust","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-8hxf-qr8p-62x4","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115906","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/ec265db0b0602f8ffb9479327397bddefb7e2216","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.0"],"description":"zip: AES Entry HMAC Authentication Bypass on Premature EOF","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":6.5,"exploitabilityScore":2.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115906","epss":0.00151,"percentile":0.04185,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115906","cwe":"CWE-354","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115906","cwe":"CWE-1284","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"}],"fix":{"versions":["9.0.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"9.0.0","date":"2026-10-30","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.086825},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-115906","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115906","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/commit/ec265db0b0602f8ffb9479327397bddefb7e2216","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/releases/tag/v9.0.0","https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-8hxf-qr8p-62x4"],"description":"zip is a zip library for Rust that supports reading and writing simple ZIP files. From 0.6.0 until 9.0.0, the AES entry reader in src/aes.rs verifies its HMAC only when the attacker-controlled data counter reaches zero. If the underlying bounded reader reaches the real end of the archive while data_remaining is still positive, or if an encrypted entry has no payload, the reader can return a clean end of stream without reading and comparing the authentication tag. Applications using by_index_decrypt, by_name_decrypt, by_path_decrypt, or password-enabled by_index_with_options can therefore accept modified plaintext without an authentication error. This issue is fixed in version 9.0.0.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":6.5,"exploitabilityScore":2.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115906","epss":0.00151,"percentile":0.04185,"date":"2026-10-30"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-115906","cwe":"CWE-354","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-115906","cwe":"CWE-1284","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"rust-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"rust","namespace":"github:language:rust","package":{"name":"zip","version":"8.6.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-8hxf-qr8p-62x4","versionConstraint":">=0.6.0,<9.0.0 (unknown)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"9.0.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index#zip@8.6.0","name":"zip","version":"8.6.0","type":"rust-crate","locations":null,"language":"rust","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:cargo/zip@8.6.0","upstreams":[]}}],"source":{"type":"sbom-file","target":"sbom/fds.cdx.json"},"distro":{"name":"","version":"","idLike":null},"descriptor":{"name":"grype","version":"0.121.0","configuration":{"output":["json"],"file":"","pretty":false,"distro":"","add-cpes-if-none":false,"output-template-file":"","check-for-app-update":true,"only-fixed":false,"only-notfixed":false,"ignore-wontfix":"","platform":"","search":{"scope":"squashed","unindexed-archives":false,"indexed-archives":true},"ignore":[{"vulnerability":"","include-aliases":false,"reason":"","namespace":"","fix-state":"","package":{"name":"kernel-headers","version":"","language":"","type":"rpm","location":"","upstream-name":"kernel"},"vex-status":"","vex-j